    <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>Sencillo Drinks Ltd ("Sencillo", "we", "us", "our") is a company registered in England and Wales. Registered office: <span class="legal-todo">[TODO: Your registered company address]</span>. Company number: <span class="legal-todo">[TODO: Companies House number]</span>. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:hola@sencillodrinks.com">hola@sencillodrinks.com</a>.</p>
    <p>This privacy notice explains how we collect, use, store and protect your personal information when you visit sencillodrinks.com, place an order, or otherwise interact with us. We act as the "data controller" for the personal information described below.</p>

    <h2 id="what-we-collect">2. What information we collect</h2>
    <p>We only collect information that we genuinely need. Depending on how you use the site, this may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contact and order details</strong> — your name, billing and delivery address, email address and phone number.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment information</strong> — handled by our payment processors (Stripe and Shopify Payments). We never see or store your full card number ourselves; we only receive confirmation that a payment has succeeded along with the last four digits of the card.</li>
      <li><strong>Account information</strong> — if you create an account: a password (encrypted), order history, saved addresses and any marketing preferences.</li>
      <li><strong>Browsing and device data</strong> — your IP address, browser type, device type, referring URL, pages viewed and approximate location, collected via cookies and similar technologies. See our <a href="{{ pages['cookies'].url }}">Cookie Policy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Age verification status</strong> — a flag confirming you have self-certified as 18 or over. We do not store identity documents.</li>
      <li><strong>Communications</strong> — emails, contact-form messages and any reviews or feedback you send us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="how-we-use">3. How we use your information</h2>
    <p>We use your information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Process and deliver your orders, including arranging delivery, handling returns and managing refunds.</li>
      <li>Send transactional emails such as order confirmations, dispatch notifications and delivery updates.</li>
      <li>Send marketing emails about new products, offers and brand news — but only where you've opted in. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in any marketing email or by emailing us.</li>
      <li>Provide customer service and respond to your enquiries.</li>
      <li>Operate, secure, monitor and improve the website and our products.</li>
      <li>Detect, prevent and investigate fraud, abuse and unlawful activity.</li>
      <li>Comply with our legal and regulatory obligations (including age-restricted sale of alcohol and HMRC record-keeping).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="legal-basis">4. Legal basis for processing</h2>
    <p>UK GDPR requires us to have a lawful basis for processing your personal information. Depending on the activity, we rely on one or more of the following:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contract</strong> — to fulfil orders you place with us and to provide our services.</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — to run, develop and secure our business, including basic analytics, fraud prevention and direct postal marketing where appropriate. We balance our interests against your privacy rights.</li>
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> — for email marketing, non-essential cookies and any optional features. You can withdraw consent at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — to comply with applicable laws, including tax, accounting and age-restricted sales regulations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="sharing">5. Who we share data with</h2>
    <p>We never sell your personal information. We share it only with trusted service providers who help us run the business, and only as far as they need it to do their job:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Payment processors</strong> — Stripe and Shopify Payments process card transactions on our behalf.</li>
      <li><strong>E-commerce platform</strong> — Shopify hosts our online store and order data.</li>
      <li><strong>Delivery couriers</strong> — Royal Mail, DPD and Evri handle delivery and need your name, address and contact details to complete it.</li>
      <li><strong>Email marketing platform</strong> — Mailchimp (Intuit Inc.) sends our newsletters and transactional order emails on our behalf.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — Google Analytics 4 (Google LLC) and Shopify Analytics help us understand how the site is used. Data is aggregated and pseudonymised.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising and retargeting</strong> — where you have given consent, Google Ads, Meta (Facebook/Instagram) Pixel, TikTok Pixel and Pinterest Tag may set cookies to measure ad performance and show you relevant Sencillo ads on other platforms.</li>
      <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong> — accountants, lawyers and auditors where needed.</li>
      <li><strong>Authorities</strong> — where we are required to do so by law, regulation or a valid legal request.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="international">6. International transfers</h2>
    <p>Some of our service providers operate outside the UK and the European Economic Area (for example in the United States). Where this is the case, we make sure appropriate safeguards are in place — typically the UK International Data Transfer Agreement, the EU Standard Contractual Clauses with the UK Addendum, or reliance on an adequacy decision recognised by the UK government. You can ask us for a copy of the relevant safeguards.</p>

    <h2 id="retention">7. How long we keep data</h2>
    <p>We keep your personal information only for as long as we need it for the purposes set out above. In practice:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Order records</strong> — kept for at least 7 years to meet HMRC and accounting obligations.</li>
      <li><strong>Account data</strong> — kept until you ask us to delete your account or close it.</li>
      <li><strong>Marketing data</strong> — kept until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete it. We periodically review our list and remove inactive contacts.</li>
      <li><strong>Support correspondence</strong> — kept for up to 3 years after the issue is resolved.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> — typically aggregated or anonymised within 14 months.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>When we no longer need your data, we securely delete or anonymise it.</p>

    <h2 id="your-rights">8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal information we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — ask us to correct anything that's inaccurate or incomplete.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your personal information, subject to legal retention rules.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — ask us to limit how we use your information in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your information in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interests, including direct marketing.</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — where we rely on consent, you can withdraw it at any time.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise any of these rights, email us at <a href="mailto:hola@sencillodrinks.com">hola@sencillodrinks.com</a>. We'll respond within one month.</p>
    <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk">ico.org.uk</a> if you think we've handled your data improperly. We'd appreciate the chance to put things right first, though.</p>

    <h2 id="cookies">9. Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use cookies and similar technologies to operate the site, remember your preferences, and (with your consent) measure usage and personalise marketing. For the full list of cookies we use and how to manage them, see our <a href="{{ pages['cookies'].url }}">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="children">10. Children</h2>
    <p>Our site sells age-restricted products and is intended for adults aged 18 or over. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us and we will delete it promptly.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this privacy policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or the law. When we do, we'll update the "last updated" date at the top of the page. Material changes will be flagged on the site or by email where appropriate.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">12. Contact us</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions about this policy or how we handle your personal information, please get in touch:</p>
    <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hola@sencillodrinks.com">hola@sencillodrinks.com</a><br>
    <strong>Post:</strong> Sencillo Drinks Ltd, <span class="legal-todo">[TODO: Your registered company address]</span>, United Kingdom</p>

  </div>
